# Test: macro-error with AST node for precise error location
#
# This test verifies that macro-error correctly uses the span from the
# provided AST node to report errors at the exact source location.

# Define a macro that validates its argument and errors with span if invalid
[macro expect-int [let arg]
  [if [int? arg]
    arg
    [macro-error "expected an integer literal" arg]]]

# Call the macro with an invalid argument (a string instead of int)
# The error should point to the "hello" argument location
[expect-int "hello"]
=== error
[E080] macro 'expect-int' expansion result failed to evaluate: macro expansion error: expected an integer literal (defined at 13:1-13:21)
  in [builtin-macro-error ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:3259:5-3259:47
   |
  3259 |     [builtin-macro-error message [first node]]]]
       |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in [builtin-if ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:2461:71-2461:89
   |
  2461 | if@[doc: "Conditional (select branch by condition)"]: [fn [let c t e] [builtin-if c t e]]
       |                                                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in materialized at 13:1-13:21
  in [if ...] at 7:3-9:53
  in macro:expect-int at 13:1-13:21
  in in expansion of `expect-int` at 13:1-13:21
